@Roy
Yes, it is safe to remove V2-V8.
Only OPEN_API_SEARCH_HOTEL_CONTENTS_V9 is currently used by the application.

@Roy Just to clarify, do you mean creating a task to document the purpose and status of each OPEN_API_SEARCH_HOTEL_CONTENTS version (V2-V9), and to clearly identify which versions can be cleaned up?

I did another check and found that V2-V8 were last updated around July 2024. They appear to be very outdated and were likely experimental versions created by the Traport team in the past. Since then, the system has only been using V9.

Given that, it seems a task to remove V2-V8 and document the current state/history of these versions would be sufficient.

@Roy
I have created a ticket to remove this.
https://ohmyjira.atlassian.net/browse/ELS-2272

@Calvin As you mentioned below, I asked because if we organize the current state and create a task with the available context, even if some details are not perfectly accurate, it will help us define the action items we need to take next.

